hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1023","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb and Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, they said: Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, On the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer, let him cancel it.” Doubt and build on certainty. If he is completely certain, he should prostrate two prostrations. If his prayer was complete, the rak’ah is voluntary and the two prostrations are voluntary. “It was incomplete. The rak’ah was complete for his prayer, and the two prostrations made the devil’s nose suffocate.”"
